hadiths[11]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2220","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) appointed a man as the leader of a military expedition. When that man led the prayer, he would always complete his recitation with (Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad). When they returned, they mentioned this to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ask him why he does this."" The people asked him, and he said (that I recite it frequently because) it describes the attributes of the Most Merciful (i.e., Allah), and I love to recite it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tell him that Allah loves him."
"2221","Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no one more patient upon hearing something hurtful than Allah; people attribute a son to Him, yet He grants them well-being and provides for them."
"2222","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to say: ""O Lord! I seek refuge in Your honor, there is no true deity except You. O Lord, only You do not die, all the jinn and mankind will die."
"2223","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""When Allah created the creation, He wrote in His Book—regarding Himself, and that Book is with Him above the Throne—that My mercy prevails over My wrath."
"2224","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): He said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “(Allah Almighty says:) I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me. If he remembers Me in his heart, I also remember him in My heart, and if he remembers Me in a gathering, I also remember him in a gathering (i.e., of angels) better than them. And if he comes near to Me a hand’s span, I go near to him an arm’s length, and if he comes near to Me an arm’s length, I go near to him two arm’s lengths, and if he comes to Me walking, I go to him running.”"
"2225","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says that when My servant intends to do an evil deed, (O angels!) do not record it until he does it. Then if he does it, write it as one evil deed, and if he refrains from it out of fear of Me (i.e., does not commit that evil), then record it as one good deed. And when he intends to do a good deed but does not do it, record it as one good deed, and if he does it, then record it from ten times up to seven hundred times."
"2226","Narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When a servant reaches a sin,"" and at times he said: ""When he commits a sin and says: O Lord! I have sinned,"" and at times he said (he says): ""I have reached a sin,"" then Allah Almighty says: My servant knows that (there is) his Lord who forgives his sins and takes him to account (from whose fear he seeks refuge). I have forgiven My servant. Then (after a short while) the servant again reaches a sin or commits a sin and says: O Lord! I have sinned or I have reached a sin, so forgive me. Allah Almighty says: My servant knows that his Lord is the One who forgives sins and also takes to account. I have forgiven My servant. Then (after a short while) he again commits a sin or said: ""reaches a sin"" and says: O Lord! I have reached a sin or I have committed a sin, so forgive me. Allah Almighty says: My servant knows that surely his Lord is the One who forgives sins and takes to account. I have forgiven My servant, so let him do what he wishes."" (The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said this) three times."
"2227","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: When the Day of Resurrection comes, I will intercede (that Allah may save people from the terrors of the Plain of Gathering and begin the reckoning), and I will say: O Lord! Admit into Paradise those who have faith equal to a mustard seed in their hearts. So those people will be admitted. Then I will say: (O Allah!) Admit into Paradise those who have (and he indicated with his finger) even a tiny bit of faith in their hearts. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: It is as if I am seeing the blessed finger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) (with which he indicated)."
"2228","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) has added to the lengthy hadith about the intercession of Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), which has already been mentioned before, as follows: ""So the people will go to ‘Isa (peace be upon him) (for intercession). He will say, 'I am not worthy of it, but you should go to Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).' So the people will come to me, and I will say, 'Yes, I am worthy of it,' and then I will seek permission to present myself before my Lord. I will be granted permission, and He will inspire me with praises and glorifications with which I will praise Him, and those (praises) I do not remember now. And I will fall down in prostration before Him. It will be said, 'O Muhammad! Raise your head and speak, you will be heard; ask, you will be given; and intercede, your intercession will be accepted.' I will say, 'O my Lord! My Ummah, my Ummah.' It will be said, 'Take out from Hell whoever has faith equal to a grain of barley in his heart.' So I will go and take them out, and then return, and again I will praise and glorify Him with the same praises, and fall down in prostration. It will be said, 'O Muhammad! Raise your head and speak, you will be heard; ask, you will be given; and intercede, your intercession will be accepted.' I will say, 'O my Lord! My Ummah, my Ummah.' It will be said, 'Take out from Hell whoever has faith equal to a particle or a mustard seed in his heart.' So I will go and take them out, and then return, and again I will praise and glorify Him with the same praises, and fall down in prostration. It will be said, 'O Muhammad! Raise your head and speak, you will be heard; ask, you will be given; and intercede, your intercession will be accepted.' I will say, 'O my Lord! My Ummah, my Ummah.' It will be said, 'Go and take out from Hell those in whose hearts is even less than a mustard seed, very little faith.' So I will go and take them out as well."
"2229","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) in another narration (that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:): ""Then I will come for the fourth time and will praise and glorify Allah with the same praises, and then I will fall into prostration. It will be said: O Muhammad! Raise your head and speak, you will be heard; ask, you will be given; intercede, your intercession will be accepted. I will say: O my Lord! Grant me permission for those people who have said 'La ilaha illallah' (there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah). Allah will say: By My honor, majesty, greatness, and magnificence, I will surely take out from Hell those who have said 'La ilaha illallah'."
"2230","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There are two phrases which are beloved to Allah, light on the tongue, and heavy on the scale (in terms of reward). (They are): (Subhan Allah wa bihamdihi, Subhan Allah al-Azeem)."" I declare Allah free from all defects and praise Him. Surely, the Most Great Allah is free from all defects."
